link/MAVSDK/issues/937", "id": 567440483, "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NzQ0MDQ4Mw==", "user": {"login": "itrigitech", "id": 54359274, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzU5Mjc0", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54359274?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech", "html_url": "https://github.com/itrigitech", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/itrigitech/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2019-12-19T10:54:46Z", "updated_at": "2019-12-19T10:55:15Z", "body": "I don't know how it works but i could imagine the message sent if the airspeed sensor is present,  in Mavlink documentation says \"Metrics typically displayed on a HUD for fixed wing aircraft.\" \r\nAnyway, testing with gazebo multicopter i see the VFR_HUD message sent so i imagine it depends more in the fact of the sensor being present or not.\r\n\r\nI think it's a good idea to add it to the telemetry plugin then. For some drones this information is very important so i will try to add it when i have time. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/567440483/reactions", "total_count": 2, "+1": 2, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_githu